 # Transvoxel Smooth Terrain Texturing
 
+Also called: Surface Color Blending
 
 ## Overview
-This method applies triplanar texturing to surfaces extracted by the Transvoxel algorithm for terrain rendering, blending "top" and "side" textures (or a material array) using a "topness" factor derived from the surface normal [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Transvoxel](6277-transvoxel.md) for geometry generation [S1, unofficial].
+This method calculates the surface color of a terrain sample extracted by the Transvoxel algorithm based on block type, slope, and procedural noise, blending between grass, stone, and forest colors [S2, unofficial]. It differs from standard single-texture approaches by using triplanar mapping to avoid UV seams on complex geometry and blending multiple material types (e.g., grass, dirt, rock) dynamically based on vertex attributes and world position [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** Vertex position in local space (`VERTEX`), vertex normal in local space (`NORMAL`), model matrix (`MODEL_MATRIX`), view matrix (`VIEW_MATRIX`), inverse view matrix (`INV_VIEW_MATRIX`), texture samplers (`u_texture_top`, `u_texture_sides`, or `u_albedo_array`), and parameters (`triplanar_sharpness = 8.0`, `topness_midlevel = 0.5`, `topness_smoothness = 0.04`) [S1, unofficial].
